          %h3#by_reduction_from_10d11d_supergravity By reduction from 10d/11d supergravity
          %p
            The following references discuss construction of full 7d sugra theories or of their solutions by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} KK-reduction
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            or from 10d
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
          %p
            The construction of 7d supergravity by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-reduction"} KK-reduction
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            was first indicated in
          %ul
            %li#FreundRubin80
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freund"}> Peter Freund
              , M. A. Rubin,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Dynamics Of Dimensional Reduction
              %strong 97
              2 (1980) 233-235 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(80)90590-0"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(80)90590-0
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            via what is now called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freund-Rubin+compactification"} Freund-Rubin compactification
          %p That their Ansatz is indeed consistent has been shown in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Horatiu+Nastase"}> Horatiu Nastase
                , Diana Vaman,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+van+Nieuwenhuizen"} Peter van Nieuwenhuizen
                %em
                  Consistent nonlinear KK reduction of 11d supergravity on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi AdS
                          %mn 7
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_7\times S_4
                  and self-duality in odd dimensions
                Phys.Lett. B469 (1999) 96-102 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9905075"}> arXiv:hep-th/9905075
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ali+Chamseddine"}> Ali Chamseddine
                , W. A. Sabra,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mn 7
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=7
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                    gauged supergravity from
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mn 10
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=10
                    supergravity
              %p
                %strong 476
                3-4 (2000) 415-419 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9911180"}> arXiv:hep-th/9911180
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0370-2693(00)00129-5"} doi:10.1016/S0370-2693(00)00129-5
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 5
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(5,\mathbb{Z})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
            in 7d is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#KumarVafa96
              %p
                Alok Kumar,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                = succeed "," do
                  %em U-Manifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9611007"} arXiv:hep-th/9611007
            %li#Rozali97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moshe+Rozali"}> Moshe Rozali
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Matrix Theory and U-Duality in Seven Dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9702136"} arXiv:hep-th/9702136
          %p Explicit compactifications are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+van+Nieuwenhuizen"}> Peter van Nieuwenhuizen
                , N. P. Warner,
                %em New Compactificafions of Ten and Eleven Dimensional Supergravity on Manifolds Which Are Not Direct Products
                Commun. Math. Phys. 99, 141-151 (1985)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jerome+Gauntlett"}> Jerome Gauntlett
                , Nakwoo Kim, Stathis Pakis,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Waldram"} Daniel Waldram
                %em M-Theory solutions with AdS factors
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0202184"}> arXiv:hep-th/0202184
                )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giuseppe+Dibitetto"}> Giuseppe Dibitetto
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicol%C3%B2+Petri"} Nicolò Petri
              = succeed "," do
                %em BPS objects in D=7 supergravity and their M-theory origin
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.06152"} arxiv:1707.06152
          %p
            Relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/massive+type+IIA+supergravity"} massive type IIA supergravity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
          %ul
            %li
